{"id":"fbf625e2-632b-439b-8115-3871a739758a","object":"chat.completion","created":1793330571,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Fixing the remaining pieces: environ error text, formatter truncation + config wiring, and stats queue `extra`.\n\n```python\nlg = read_file(\"deepinfer/logger.py\")\nlh = lg['file_hash']\nsl = read_file(\"deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py\")\nsh = sl['file_hash']\nev = read_file(\"deepinfer/environ.py\")\neh = ev['file_hash']\n\n# 1. environ: error text includes variable name, int parse errors wrapped\nr1 = replace_text(\"deepinfer/environ.py\", '''def _log_max_message_chars(v: str | None) -> int | None:\n    if v is None:\n        return None\n    value = int(v)\n    if value < 32:\n        raise ValueError(f\"must be >= 32, got {value!r}\")\n    return value''', '''_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS_NAME = \"DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS\"\n_MIN_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = 32\n\n\ndef _log_max_message_chars(v: str | None) -> int | None:\n    if v is None:\n        return None\n    try:\n        value = int(v)\n    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"{_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS_NAME} must be an integer >= {_MIN_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS}, \"\n            f\"got {v!r}\"\n        ) from None\n    if value < _MIN_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS:\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"{_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS_NAME} must be >= {_MIN_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS}, got {value!r}\"\n        )\n    return value''', eh)\nprint(\"environ\", r1.get('rc', r1))\n\n# 2a. logger: apply budget to message body only, without touching shared record fields\nr2 = replace_text(\"deepinfer/logger.py\", '''    def format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        msg = super().format(record)\n        # 快速路径：单行日志（绝大多数情况）无需做对齐处理''', '''    def format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        saved_msg: object = None\n        saved_args: object = None\n        truncated = False\n        if self.max_message_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n            # 先完成 %s 等参数替换，再对消息正文做长度预算\n            message = record.getMessage()\n            if len(message) > self.max_message_chars:\n                saved_msg, saved_args = record.msg, record.args\n                record.msg = _truncate_message(message, self.max_message_chars)\n                record.args = None\n                truncated = True\n        try:\n            msg = super().format(record)\n        finally:\n            if truncated:\n                # 不改写共享的原记录，随后交给完整处理器仍是完整消息\n                record.msg, record.args = saved_msg, saved_args\n        # 快速路径：单行日志（绝大多数情况）无需做对齐处理''', lh)\nprint(\"logger.format\", r2.get('rc', r2))\n\n# 2b. logger: default init reads the centralized config\nlg2 = read_file(\"deepinfer/logger.py\")\nr3 = replace_text(\"deepinfer/logger.py\", '''    fmt = NewLineFormatter(\n        _FORMAT,\n        datefmt=_DATE_FORMAT,\n        use_color=sys.stdout.isatty(),\n    )''', '''    from deepinfer.environ import envs\n\n    fmt = NewLineFormatter(\n        _FORMAT,\n        datefmt=_DATE_FORMAT,\n        use_color=sys.stdout.isatty(),\n        max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS,\n    )''', lg2['file_hash'])\nprint(\"logger.setup\", r3.get('rc', r3))\n\n# 3. stats_logger: keep stats messages complete via logging extra\nr4 = replace_text(\"deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py\", '''            for m in msgs:\n                logger.info(m)''', '''            for m in msgs:\n                logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})''', sh)\nprint(\"stats\", r4.get('rc', r4))\n```","reasoning_content":"Progress: environ.py and logger.py changed. Need to: (1) fix environ error messages to include variable name, (2) add truncation logic in logger.format (currently _truncate_message exists but format doesn't apply it), (3) setup_logger should pass max_message_chars from config, (4) stats_logger logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True}).\n\nLet me check logger format — currently format doesn't use max_message_chars. Need to add truncation of record.message before/after formatting. Best approach: override format to operate on record.message before super().format()? But must not mutate shared record. Standard approach: temporarily set record.msg to truncated message and restore. Let's implement:\n\n```python\n    def format(self, record):\n        max_chars = self.max_message_chars\n        if max_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n            # compute message with args substituted without mutating record\n            message = record.getMessage()\n            if len(message) > max_chars:\n                truncated = _truncate_message(message, max_chars)\n                saved = (record.msg, record.args)\n                record.msg = truncated\n                record.args = None\n                try:\n                    msg = super().format(record)\n                finally:\n                    record.msg, record.args = saved\n                ... continue with newline prefix and color\n```\n\nBut record.message is cached by Formatter.format (sets record.message). Actually logging.Formatter.format sets record.message = record.getMessage(). Since we restore msg/args after, record.message stays as truncated text. Careful: it should be fine but subsequent full handler: record.msg and args restored, then next formatter recomputes record.message via getMessage again — it sets record.message each time, so fine.\n\nAlso traceback exc_info: super().format with exc_info appends traceback text. That's fine since budget only applies to message body.\n\nLet me restructure format method cleanly:\n\n```python\n    def format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        saved: tuple[object, object] | None = None\n        if self.max_message_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n            message = record.getMessage()\n            if len(message) > self.max_message_chars:\n                saved = (record.msg, record.args)\n                record.msg = _truncate_message(message, self.max_message_chars)\n                record.args = None\n        try:\n            msg = super().format(record)\n        finally:\n            if saved is not None:\n                record.msg, record.args = saved\n        if \"\\n\" in msg and record.message:\n            ...\n```\n\nWait — record.message after restore: record.message will be the truncated message when saved... Actually with saved not None, super().format computes record.message = getMessage() = truncated msg (args None). After restore, record.message remains truncated string. Then in the newline step, `msg.find(record.message)` uses truncated message which occurs in msg as prefix start. That's fine — but to be safe, use saved message. Actually when truncation happened, record.message is truncated text which is contained in msg. OK.\n\nBut hmm, for multi-line messages, the truncation keeping head/tail may include newlines; the prefix replacement for newlines could break the character budget? Budget applies to message body, prefix alignment adds prefix to newlines, not counted. Acceptable.\n\nAlso after restore record.message should maybe be reset to full? For downstream handler, logging.Formatter.format always recomputes record.message, so no issue.\n\nNow _setup_logger: pass max_message_chars. Need import of envs in logger.py — careful about circular imports: does environ import logger? environ imports os, threading only. logger.py importing from deepinfer.environ should be fine. But there might be a circular import if deepinfer/__init__.py... Let's do lazy import inside _setup_logger:\n\n```python\nfrom deepinfer.environ import envs\n```\ninside function to be safe.\n\nAlso fix environ error message to include variable name: `DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS must be an integer >= 32, got ...`. Also empty string: int(\"\") raises ValueError with message \"invalid literal for int() with base 10: ''\" which doesn't contain var name. So wrap.\n\nLet me update _log_max_message_chars:\n\n```python\n_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS_ENV = \"DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS\"\n\n\ndef _log_max_message_chars(v: str | None) -> int | None:\n    if v is None:\n        return None\n    try:\n        value = int(v)\n    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n        raise ValueError(f\"{_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS_ENV} must be an integer >= 32, got {v!r}\") from None\n    if value < 32:\n        raise ValueError(f\"{_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS_ENV} must be >= 32, got {value!r}\")\n    return value\n```\n\nHmm, but maybe the test expects the error from EnvVar descriptor to be wrapped. Let me check descriptor code to see how conversion errors are wrapped. Let me read the EnvVar class region.\n\nAlso need stats_logger edit. Let's read environ EnvVar class region (lines 40-100) and the current logger.format snippet already known.\n\nI'll do reads + edits in one action where possible (multiple statements allowed). Reads first then edits based on content — but I can't branch on content in same block reliably... I can print and edit in the same block since I know the current content of logger.py precisely from evidence. For environ's EnvVar class, I need to see how __get__ wraps ValueError. Let's just read it and edit logger/stats in the same action.\n\nLet's do:\n- read environ lines 33-100\n- edit logger format\n- edit logger _setup_logger\n- edit stats_logger logger.info\n\nCareful about hash usage: use l['file_hash'] from read in same block? Instead re-read files to get current hashes: I'll use read_range for logger.format region to get hash, or use read_file. Simpler: read logger.py file (hash known ac8e... but need exact). Use returned dict.\n\nPlan block:\n\n```python\nenv_block = read_range(\"deepinfer/environ.py\", 33, 100)\nprint(env_block['content'])\nlg = read_file(\"deepinfer/logger.py\")\nh = lg['file_ha